# bridge_config.shellnet — per-network profile for `ackinacki-bridge`.
#
# WHAT IT IS
# ----------
# One-of-N profile files consumed by the `ackinacki-bridge` CLI. The CLI
# auto-sources the file pointed to by the `BRIDGE_CONFIG` env var at
# startup (before clap resolves --flag / env= defaults). Precedence:
#     explicit --flag > shell env > profile file > compiled default.
#
# Ships alongside `bridge_config.local` (devnet) and
# `bridge_config.mainnet` (placeholder). `bridge_config` (no suffix) is
# a symlink to this file — that's the pinned default for third-party
# users of the shellnet reference deploy.
#
# HOW TO CONSUME
# --------------
#   cd crates/ackinacki-bridge
#   export BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x…                        # your own key
#   export BRIDGE_CONFIG=./config/bridge_config          # symlink → .shellnet
#   ../bridge-prover-libraries/target/release/ackinacki-bridge withdraw \
#       --from … --from-keys … --to … --to-chain 11155111 --amount 1.000000
#
# Switching networks is a one-liner:
#   export BRIDGE_CONFIG=./config/bridge_config.local
#
# BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY is deliberately NOT in this file — it is per-operator,
# not per-network. Export it in your shell (or a personal, git-ignored env
# file) before invoking the CLI. See README.md "Quick start" for wallet
# creation + Sepolia funding via the pk910 PoW or Google Cloud Web3
# faucets. Never reuse a wallet that holds real funds; never commit the
# private key.
#
# Relative paths below are anchored to the working directory
# `crates/ackinacki-bridge/`.

# --- Ethereum side (Sepolia) --------------------------------------------------
RPC_URL=https://ethereum-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com

# --- Acki Nacki side (shellnet) -----------------------------------------------
NETWORK=shellnet.ackinacki.org
BRIDGE_GQL_ENDPOINT=https://shellnet.ackinacki.org/graphql

# On-chain USDCBridge account id (64 hex, no `0x`). The dapp_id is
# resolved live via GraphQL, so only the account id is needed here.
#
# This value is NOT free-form: `withdrawByProof` compares the pair
# (dappFr, accFr) it derives from a proof against the pair the deploy
# was pinned to at construction, BEFORE verifying the proof itself, so
# a mismatch is a refusal after the burn. Preflight checks it up front
# for that reason — and it means the id here has to match the deploy in
# BRIDGE_ADDRESS below, not merely be a real account.
#
# It can always be read back from the deploy rather than looked up:
#
#   cast call $BRIDGE_ADDRESS 'bridgeWithdrawalAccFr()(uint256)' --rpc-url $RPC_URL
#
# `accFr` is these same 32 bytes read big-endian (and below the BN254
# field prime, so the reading is unambiguous): print it as 064x and you
# have the value for this line.
#
# NODE-4011 briefly moved this to `20f9338d…d7c3c5b8` over a new
# eccUSDCBridge and was rolled back the same day. Both deploys exist and
# both answer; only the one the relayer advances is usable, and the
# check below is what tells them apart.
USDC_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT_ID=1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a1a

# Partner-provided bridge-owner key for `USDCBridge.mintAndSend`. Used
# only by `scripts/deploy_msig_and_mint.py` to seed a fresh multisig
# with 1 USDC on ECC[3]. The Rust CLI does not read this.
USDC_BRIDGE_KEY_PATH=../bridge-prover-libraries/python/contracts/USDCBridge.shellnet.keys.json

# --- L2 anchor selection ------------------------------------------------------
# The pinned shellnet deploy is L2-anchored (anchor_level=2); the CLI
# refuses to talk to it without the anchor flag, and --i-know-the-wait
# acknowledges the ~91 min per-bundle L2 cadence that stage 4b
# (wait-for-coverage) may block on.
BRIDGE_ANCHOR_LAYER=2
BRIDGE_I_KNOW_THE_WAIT=true

# --- local dirs ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `params/` holds ~17 GB of SRS + per-circuit vk/pk files, shared with
# the bundle daemon. Do NOT wipe — keygen would re-burn ~7 min per
# circuit.
BRIDGE_PARAMS_DIR=../bridge-prover-libraries/params

# pk cache dir passed through to the C4 aggregator subprocess.
BRIDGE_PK_CACHE_DIR=../bridge-prover-libraries/params/pk_cache

# Per-withdrawal working directory (bundle_out, per-run logs).
BRIDGE_WORK_DIR=./work_dir

# Aggregator scratch dir. Must be an absolute path resolvable from the
# aggregate-proof subprocess CWD — the shell wrappers turn this into an
# absolute path before invoking cargo run.
BRIDGE_SNARK_DIR=./work_dir/shplonk-snark

# Where per-withdrawal idempotency state files live. Defaults to
# `$HOME/.bridge-withdraw-state/` if unset; kept per-user, survives
# tree moves (see `src/orchestrator.rs::default_state_dir`).
BRIDGE_WITHDRAW_STATE_DIR=./withdraw-state

# --- SHPLONK aggregation (mandatory) ------------------------------------------
# The on-chain AckiNackiBridge verifier only accepts aggregated calldata.
# The CLI refuses to submit without both dirs resolving.
BRIDGE_AGGREGATOR_DIR=../bridge-evm-aggregator
BRIDGE_VERIFIERS_DIR=../../contracts/ethereum/verifiers

# --- Deploy target ------------------------------------------------------------
# Currently pinned to the shellnet team's L2-anchored reference deploy
# on Sepolia. The server-side bundle relayer that advances this contract
# runs L2 only. See README.md Quick start for the default-user flow.
#
# NODE-4011 moved this to `0x8545129b215B248944A3aE40f711F34CAb458644`
# over a new AN-side eccUSDCBridge and rolled back the same day. That
# deploy still exists and still answers every getter — which is exactly
# why an address alone proves nothing. VERIFY BEFORE A RUN THAT COSTS
# MONEY, because a bridge nobody advances takes the burn and then times
# out at stage 4b:
#
#   cast call $BRIDGE_ADDRESS 'storedLastSeenBlockSeqNo()(uint64)' --rpc-url $RPC_URL
#   TIP=$(cast block-number --rpc-url $RPC_URL)
#   cast logs --address $BRIDGE_ADDRESS --from-block $((TIP - 10000)) \
#     'BlockVerified(uint256,uint64,uint8,uint8)' --rpc-url $RPC_URL \
#     | grep -E '^  blockNumber' | tail -3
#
# Bundles land ~437 Sepolia blocks apart (~87 min); a last event older
# than that means this deploy is not the live one — check with the team
# before blaming the daemon.
#
# Changing this line means changing USDC_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT_ID above with
# it: a deploy is pinned to one AN-side bridge account, and the two are
# checked against each other in preflight. A deploy also carries its own
# treasury — `treasuryBalance` is a counter on the bridge itself, moved
# only by `deposit`, so a plain USDC transfer to this address funds
# nothing, and a switch does not bring the balance along. See README
# Step 3.
#
# Advanced users who ran their own `deploy_bridge_bundle.sh` should
# overwrite this with the `BRIDGE_ADDRESS` from their own
# `L{1,2}_config/env` — see `docs/advanced_user_withdraw_runbook.md`
# Step L1. L1 is testing-only; L2 is the production shape.
#
# Comment out to force the CLI to fail loudly ("missing required
# argument BRIDGE_ADDRESS") instead of silently connecting to the wrong
# bridge.
BRIDGE_ADDRESS=0x0F4F8b7EF2E40587ff1cC5d3393b9c1Fb8f02fc7
